  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-7" type="10">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ministry of Foreign Affairs of the Netherlands</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Learning and Research programme for the &#x2018;Policy Framework Strengthening Civil Society&#x2019;</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Linking and Learning, Research, Networking and Communication linked to the implementation of the Policy Framework Strengthening Civil Society to be implemented in a selection of 10 countries in collaboration with relevant missions, partners and thematic departments. In November 2019 the Ministry of Foreign Affairs published the grant instrument &#x2018;Policy Framework for Strengthening Civil Society&#x2019;. Under this grant instrument, a total of 42 new partnerships started their 5-year programmes on 1 January 2021 (to 31 December 2025), in a total of 65 countries. Three other instruments are also part of the SCS-policy: Leading from the South, Voice and the Civic Space Fund (including Flex Option) also provide funding for local networks and initiatives under this framework. The approved SCS MEL plan includes a learning programme that has five components: 1) Dialogues (globally) 2) Basic Course SCS 3) Linking &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; Learning 4) (action) research and innovation 5) networking and communication. The facilitation of global Dialogues has already been outsourced to a company called Aprilli, who already facilitated the first SCS dialogue in June and a second one is planned for November. This has been contracted from operational budgets until 2023. A course provider has been contracted to develop and pilot the Basic Course Civil Society Strengthening with a first batch of 75 students. The number of people registering exceeded 300 and therefore a waiver to continue with the same course provider after successful completion of the pilot will be pursued (activity number 4000005095) . MFA launches a European tender procedure to invite contractors for the development of a learning and research programme under the Policy Framework for Strengthening Civil Society that caters for the remaining three components of the learning programme. The main objectives of this programme are to: 1. Providing space to partners and Missions of the Ministry to reflect on the existing practice of lobby and advocacy towards governments, companies and citizens and outcomes thereof in terms of their contributions to the achievement of the Sustainable Development Goals in 2030. 2. Engage the national and southern knowledge systems in developing the evidence base that supports lobby and advocacy by formulating learning questions and commissioning research assignments linked to the Strengthening Civil Society programme; 3. Ensure effective feedback from learning and research activities to the ongoing lobby and advocacy practice of both the CSOs and the Ministry and to new policy preparation processes within the Ministry focussing on Strengthening Civil Society.</narrative>
  </description>
